        <mxCell id="SfDgYsewkCgwbqOTThhK-4" parent="SfDgYsewkCgwbqOTThhK-1" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;rotatable=0;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;+ TickComponent(DeltaTime: float): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ ToggleBuildMode(bEnable: bool): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ SetBuildLibraryData(NewData: UBuildLibraryData*): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ SelectBuildingFromLibrary(IndexToSelect: int32): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ PlaceBuildObject(): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;+ RotateBuildObject(Direction: float): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;# BeginPlay(): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- UpdateGhost(ViewLocation: FVector&amp;amp;): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- UpdateGhostMaterial(): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- LoadGhostMeshAsync(): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- OnGhostMeshLoaded(LoadedData: TWeakObjectPtr&amp;lt;UBuildObjectData&amp;gt;): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- LoadBuildDataAsync(IndexToLoad: int32): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- OnBuildDataLoaded(IndexToLoad: int32): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- LoadBuildClassAsync(): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- PlaceBuildObjectOnLoaded(LoadedData: TWeakObjectPtr&amp;lt;UBuildObjectData&amp;gt;): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- TryPlaceBuildObject(): void&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- GetPlacementLocation(): FVector&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- CheckPlacement(Location: FVector&amp;amp;): bool&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- HasGround(Location: const FVector&amp;amp;, GroundHit: FHitResult&amp;amp;, ExtentHeight: const float): bool&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- IsTooDeep(Location: const FVector&amp;amp;, GroundHit: const FHitResult&amp;amp;, ExtentHeight: const float): bool&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- IsBlocked(Location: const FVector&amp;amp;, MeshComp: UStaticMeshComponent*): bool&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- AlignPlacement(Location: FVector&amp;amp;, GroundHit: const FHitResult&amp;amp;, ExtentHeight: const float): void&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="462" width="560" y="358" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SfDgYsewkCgwbqOTThhK-5" parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;h3 dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;UConstructionComponent - Explanation&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;ToggleBuildMode(bEnable)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Enabling turns on the component&#39;s tick. Disabling clears the current selection, hides the ghost, removes its mesh and stops the tick.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;SetBuildLibraryData(NewData)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Gives the component the library of available buildings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;SelectBuildingFromLibrary(Index)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Validates the index and starts an async load of that building&#39;s data. The building becomes the current selection only after loading finishes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;PlaceBuildObject()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Entry point for placing. If the building&#39;s actor class isn&#39;t loaded yet, it loads it first and places afterwards; otherwise it places immediately. Does nothing until the ghost has been built for the current selection.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;TryPlaceBuildObject()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Spawns the real building at &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;FinalSnappedLocation&lt;/code&gt; if placement is valid, then re-checks placement, because the spot is now occupied.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;RotateBuildObject(Direction)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Changes the yaw by &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;RotateRate * Direction&lt;/code&gt; and refreshes the ghost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;UpdateGhost(ViewLocation)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Creates the ghost actor if missing and reloads its mesh when the selection changed. While the mesh is loading the ghost stays hidden; otherwise it moves and rotates the ghost, validates placement and updates its color. Despite the parameter name, &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;ViewLocation&lt;/code&gt; is the grid-snapped point, not the camera position.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;UpdateGhostMaterial()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Green and semi-transparent when placement is valid, red and more opaque when it isn&#39;t.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;GetPlacementLocation()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Takes the point at &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;MaxBuildDistance&lt;/code&gt; along the camera&#39;s forward direction and snaps it to the building&#39;s grid. This is only a raw point in the air; no trace is done here.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;CheckPlacement(Location)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Runs the full validation: ground exists below, the object isn&#39;t sunk too deep, then aligns to the ground and checks for overlaps. Note the side effect: it also writes &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;FinalSnappedLocation&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;HasGround()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Line trace downward from slightly above the location, long enough to cover the object&#39;s half-height plus &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;MaxFloatingDistance&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;IsTooDeep()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Compares how far the object&#39;s bottom would sink into the ground with &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;GroundDigDepth&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;AlignPlacement()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Shifts the object so its bottom sits exactly on the ground hit point (plus a 0.1 offset to avoid touching) and stores the result in &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;FinalSnappedLocation&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;IsBlocked()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Overlap test using the ghost&#39;s mesh at the final location and current rotation, ignoring the owner and the ghost itself.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;LoadBuildDataAsync()&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;OnBuildDataLoaded()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Async-load the selected building&#39;s data. &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;CurrentIndexToLoad&lt;/code&gt; is used to discard the result if the player has already selected another building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;LoadGhostMeshAsync()&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;OnGhostMeshLoaded()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Load the preview mesh, apply it to the ghost and create its dynamic material. The result is ignored if the selection changed in the meantime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;LoadBuildClassAsync()&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;PlaceBuildObjectOnLoaded()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Load the building&#39;s actor class on demand when the player tries to place it, then place it if the selection is still the same.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;TickComponent()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: While build mode is active, recomputes the snapped point and updates the ghost only when that point has changed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;LastSnappedLocation&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: The last grid-snapped point. Used to skip ghost updates when nothing moved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;FinalSnappedLocation&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: The location after ground alignment, where the building will actually be placed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;RotateTarget&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Current rotation (yaw) applied to the ghost and the placed building.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;PreviousBuildData&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: The building the ghost was last built for. Comparing it with &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;CurrentBuildData&lt;/code&gt; detects a selection change.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;CurrentIndexToLoad&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Index of the most recently requested building. Used to discard stale loads.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;bGhostMeshReady&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: True once the ghost&#39;s mesh has been loaded and applied. Until then the ghost stays hidden.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;bCanPlace&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Result of the last validation. Drives the ghost&#39;s color and whether placement is allowed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;MaxBuildDistance&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;GroundDigDepth&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;MaxFloatingDistance&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: How far from the camera you can build, how deep an object may sink into the ground, and how high above it may float.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1490" width="1010" x="730" y="-630" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
